 * 3. As the owner/editor, fetch the comment edit by its ID - expect success and matching details.
 * 4. As the admin, fetch the same comment edit record - expect success, same details.
 * 5. Log in as an unrelated member and attempt to fetch the edit - expect forbidden or not found.
 * 6. Attempt to fetch a non-existent (random) UUID as edit ID - expect 404 Not Found.
 * 7. (If possible, soft-delete the comment edit and try to fetch - expect 404. If soft-delete not supported by API, this step is skipped.)
 *
 * Note: This test covers all feasible parts using the provided API. Member/admin context switching, access denial for outsiders, and soft-delete fetch testing are not possible without additional authentication or delete APIs. Documentation indicates these are intentionally skipped.
 */
export async function test_api_discussionBoard_test_get_single_comment_edit_entry_with_access_control(
